In article <1olbk6$lls@cat.cis.Brown.EDU> ST201943@brownvm.brown.edu (Jason Duva) writes:
>>The book curses items, I think both the book and the amulet summon monsters.
>
> Is it necessary to have the Book of the Dead to win the Game? Can you drop
>the book, bell, and cadellabrum down in hell after getting the Amulet, hence
>saving encumbrance, and lots of random cursings?

You're both wrong.  Simply killing the Wizard causes bad things to
happen.  The Book has no effects unless you read it.  The Amulet
increases food consumption, causes limited magic mapping (useless
after you've explored everything, which you should have), and helps
you find the portals on the elemental planes.

And no, once you open the gate to the deepest pit of Gehennom, you no
longer need the artifacts.  They are nice for summoning wraiths,
though.

